<title>ZIMBABWE: PG Industries half yr shr, div falls.</title>
<headline>PG Industries half yr shr, div falls.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended September 30</p>
<p>	    (million Zimbabwe dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		     10.68   vs 25.08</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		     3.50    vs 11.00</p>
<p>    After-tax profit	    12.99   vs 29.75</p>
<p>    Interest paid		 29.98   vs 10.52</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		12.99   vs 35.75</p>
<p>    Taxation			none    vs  6.00</p>
<p>    Turnover			326.37  vs 278.80</p>
<p>Full name: PG Industries</p>
<p>NOTE:- Directors have offered a scrip alternative to the dividend to shareholders registered on January 3.</p>
<p>They said that the group's anticipated acquisition of construction firm Johnson and Fletcher for an undisclosed amount would happen too late in the year to have any impact on the current year forecast. However, it said, better profits results were expected in the coming year.</p>
<p>----Emelia Sithole, Harare Newsroom: +263-4 72 52 27/8/9----</p>
